{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nFollow-up (fix b) to creatable-foldable-arthropods (fix a, merged a0fc8d43556 / Gerrit 1761). A second, independent defect remains in the verifier's evidence-banking path: at SEARCH EXHAUSTION, `BOUNDED_FALLBACK_EVIDENCE` banks `met=false` — i.e. \"the criterion is unmet\" — when what the run actually established is only \"the search budget ran out before sufficient evidence was found\". This misattributes absence-of-evidence as evidence-of-absence, producing false FAIL verdicts on tickets whose evidence exists but was not reached within the window.\n\n## Proposed fix\nDistinguish THREE evidence outcomes: met, refuted, and insufficient (search exhausted without a determination) — the third carried as a framework-set `evidence_sufficient:false` marker riding alongside `met:false`, per the verdict_obtainable precedent (completion.py:516; schema :14-18), so verdict/met vocabularies and every fail-closed consumer stay unchanged. The insufficiency marker must originate in the banking WRITE path, whose chokepoints are bool-typed today:\n- `CompletionEvidencePolicy.fallback_record` (completion_tool_policy.py:100-101) passes a literal `False` through the record tool — at exhaustion it must bank `met=false` PLUS the `evidence_sufficient:false` marker, via an internal write path (not the model-facing tool).\n- `CriterionBank.upsert` (completion_banking.py:441-461) — persist the optional marker alongside the bool `met` (the \"writes remain bool-only\" docstring contract updates with it).\n- `record_criterion_verdict`'s model-facing tool signature (:539) stays BOOL — the marker is exclusively the policy-side exhaustion outcome, never a model-tool input.\n- `harvest_structured_into_bank` (:583) keeps its bool gate but must carry the marker through re-harvest instead of dropping it.\n\n**Full consumer graph (all bool-coercing/validating sites change together):**\n- **Schema (`src/rebar/schemas/completion_verdict.schema.json`)**: follow the `verdict_obtainable` precedent (schema :14-18, completion.py:516) — a framework-set boolean marker riding ALONGSIDE {PASS, FAIL}, not a third token, keeping the normalizing fail-safe and every consumer's blocking behavior unchanged. Same pattern: `verdict` stays PASS/FAIL (insufficient evidence still FAILs and blocks), `met` stays bool, and two OPTIONAL framework-set markers are added: `criteria[].evidence_sufficient:false` (this false is exhaustion, not refutation) and top-level `evidence_sufficient:false` (present iff no criterion is genuinely unmet but ≥1 is insufficient). Consumers reading only verdict/met are untouched; message-rendering consumers read the marker. Both rendering seams validate against this schema (completion_recovery.py:674, :774).\n- **`_validate_coverage` (completion_recovery.py:364-368, run at :717)**: met stays bool → type gate and :370 PASS cross-check unchanged; markers must survive validation untouched.\n- **`_run_finalizer` (completion_recovery.py:741)**: the banked-evidence payload must carry the marker so the LLM finalizer sees exhaustion, not refutation.\n- **Unbanked/exhausted placeholder branches** (`assemble_deterministic_verdict` :646-660, `merge_finalizer_with_bank` :715+): a never-banked criterion at exhaustion IS absence-of-evidence — placeholders carry the marker (keeping `exhausted`) instead of a bare `met:false` + high-severity FAIL finding.\n- **`reconcile_verdict` (completion.py:495-564)**: the `:522` PASS/FAIL normalization is UNTOUCHED. Changes: preserve the framework-set markers through reconciliation, and make the `:564` remediation branch marker-aware — a FAIL carrying `evidence_sufficient:false` gets insufficient-evidence remediation (re-verify / widen scope / operator-attest) instead of unmet-criteria guidance. The `:526` verdict_obtainable fault path is unaffected: insufficient-evidence criteria still emit findings, so the no-findings heuristic never sees them.\n- **Close-gate refusal (close_precheck.py:571-589)**: still gates on non-PASS (unchanged, fail-closed) — but when the verdict carries `evidence_sufficient:false` it reports \"insufficient evidence\" + the marker's remediation instead of asserting \"N unmet criteria\".\n- **Finalizer prompt (src/rebar/llm/reviewers/completion_verifier_finalizer.md:23-28)**: currently collapses missing/truncated evidence into `met:false` + high-severity finding + FAIL — the defect at the LLM seam. Update the decision rule: banked insufficient entries echo as `met:false`, findings text says insufficient; the framework re-stamps the marker post-merge (the stamp is the enforcement, the prompt aligns the text).\n- **Completion sidecar (`completion_sidecar.py:335`)**: persists `criteria` as-is — verified pass-through; a round-trip test pins it, no code change expected.\n- **Banked-entry rendering** in `assemble_deterministic_verdict` (:619-640) and `merge_finalizer_with_bank` (:705-714): marker-carrying entries emit `met:false + evidence_sufficient:false` with an insufficient-evidence finding, not a bare unmet-criterion FAIL finding. The change is honesty of message and recorded class, never gate leniency.\n\n## Scope\n- The banking WRITE path: `fallback_record` wiring in src/rebar/llm/completion_tool_policy.py (exhaustion site), and in src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_banking.py: `CriterionBank.upsert` (persists the marker), `record_criterion_verdict` (unchanged bool tool signature — guard only), `harvest_structured_into_bank` (markers survive re-harvest), and BOTH unbanked/exhausted placeholder branches (assemble_deterministic_verdict :646-660, merge_finalizer_with_bank :715+).\n- src/rebar/schemas/completion_verdict.schema.json — optional framework-set `evidence_sufficient:false` markers (top-level + per-criterion), verdict_obtainable pattern; verdict vocabulary unchanged.\n- src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_recovery.py — `_validate_coverage` markers survive validation; `_run_finalizer` payload carries the marker (:741).\n- src/rebar/llm/completion.py — `reconcile_verdict` preserves the evidence_sufficient markers; :564 remediation branch marker-aware.\n- src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py — refusal message keys on the marker (insufficient evidence vs unmet criteria); still refuses both.\n- src/rebar/llm/reviewers/completion_verifier_finalizer.md — evidence-sufficiency decision rule (:23-28).\n- src/rebar/llm/completion_sidecar.py — verified pass-through (round-trip test only; no code change expected).\n- Tests: exhaustion banks the marker; genuine refutation stays bare met=false; rendering distinguishes the two.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] At search exhaustion, banked fallback evidence carries `evidence_sufficient:false` (never a bare `met=false`); new unit test.\n- [ ] A marker-carrying bank entry survives `harvest_structured_into_bank` round-trips; the model-facing `record_criterion_verdict` tool signature remains bool-only; unit tests.\n- [ ] A genuine positive refutation still banks `met=false` and still yields FAIL; checked by a guard test.\n- [ ] BOTH rendering seams — `assemble_deterministic_verdict` and `merge_finalizer_with_bank` — emit `met:false + evidence_sufficient:false` for insufficient-evidence entries, INCLUDING their unbanked/exhausted placeholder branches; per-seam and per-branch rendering tests.\n- [ ] Schema validates marker-carrying AND existing all-bool records; `_validate_coverage` passes markers through, still rejects untyped records; `_run_finalizer` payload carries the marker; sidecar round-trip preserves it; unit tests each.\n- [ ] Close gate still BLOCKS on insufficient evidence (verdict stays FAIL) but the refusal reports insufficient evidence + remediation, not unmet criteria; `reconcile_verdict` preserves markers + swaps remediation; gate + reconcile tests.\n- [ ] `make lint` and `make typecheck` clean; lands via Gerrit (LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1) before close.\n\n## Out of scope\nGuard/memo interaction (fix a, landed); retry policy; prompt changes OTHER than the finalizer's evidence-sufficiency rule above."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786729551615777001,"uuid":"b1f787b2-367e-46a4-91b6-2b28da95277e"}